{
  "account": "plur",
  "background": { "color": "#0A0A0A" },
  "slides": [
    {
      "type": "cover",
      "main": ["GOLDIE", "TIMELESS"],
      "sub": "The boy they put in care made a 22-minute symphony."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "Walsall, 1965.",
        "His father, Jamaican.",
        "His mother, Scottish.",
        "At three years old,",
        "he was taken into care.",
        "Moved between foster homes",
        "in Wolverhampton."
      ],
      "sub": "What happened there is in his autobiography. He wrote it down so it would exist."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "Graffiti was his first language.",
        "By his teens, a leading voice",
        "in the Midlands wildstyle scene.",
        "1988. Channel 4: Bombin'.",
        "After filming —",
        "they took him to New York."
      ],
      "sub": "He stood in front of walls he had only ever seen in photographs. Something changed."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "Back in England,",
        "he followed the bass.",
        "Grooverider's sets.",
        "Kemistry, who believed in him first.",
        "4hero at Reinforced Records,",
        "who taught him to produce."
      ],
      "sub": "1994. Metalheadz — co-founded with Kemistry and Storm."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "November 1994.",
        "Inner City Life —",
        "feat. Diane Charlemagne.",
        "UK Singles Chart: #39.",
        "UK Dance Chart: #6."
      ],
      "sub": "Drum & bass had never sounded like it was grieving for something until that moment."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "The label was nervous.",
        "\"Who is going to listen",
        "to a 21-minute track?\"",
        "August 7, 1995.",
        "Timeless.",
        "UK Albums Chart: #7."
      ],
      "sub": "Drum & bass became music that day."
    },
    {
      "type": "body",
      "text": [
        "1998. Saturnz Return.",
        "The opening track: Mother.",
        "Over 60 minutes long.",
        "A 30-piece string section.",
        "Noel Gallagher. KRS-One.",
        "No one else had tried",
        "to do any of it."
      ],
      "sub": "1999 — the boy from the care homes appeared as a villain in a James Bond film."
    },
    {
      "type": "quote",
      "quote": [
        "The same way graffiti on a wall",
        "stays in the memory —",
        "I wanted music to leave something",
        "that outlasts the moment."
      ],
      "note": "— Goldie. Save this."
    }
  ]
}
